================================================================================
2. APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE & ROUTING FLOW
================================================================================

2.1 ARCHITECTURAL PATTERN: Front-Controller & View-Presenter Hybrid
- The frontend uses a clean separation:
  - Top-level files (`home.php`, `service-detail.php`, `blog.php`) act as Controllers:
    1. Include `app/config.php` to initialize environment, session, and DB connection.
    2. Query required database records with PDO prepared statements.
    3. Aggregate stats, sanitize inputs, and set `$pageTitle` / `$metaDescription`.
    4. Delegate rendering to corresponding view in `app/Views/frontend/*.php`.
- The admin dashboard uses dedicated route files in `admin/*.php` guarded by `admin/auth.php`, which delegates views to `app/Views/admin/*.php` wrapped between `admin/includes/header-pro.php` and `footer-pro.php`.

2.2 URL REWRITING & ROUTING MATRIX (.htaccess)
- Clean URLs:
  - `/services`                 --> `services.php`
  - `/services/{slug}`          --> `service-detail.php?slug={slug}`
  - `/blogs` or `/blog`         --> `blog.php`
  - `/blogs/{slug}`             --> `blog-detail.php?slug={slug}`
  - `/admin/{route}.php`        --> 301 Redirect to `/admin/{route}` (clean extensionless URLs)
  - `/{page}`                   --> Rewritten internally to `{page}.php` if the file exists.
- Static Caching & Compression:
  - Images, WebP, SVG, Fonts    : 1-Year public immutable cache
  - CSS & JS                    : 1-Month public immutable cache
  - HTML, PHP, JSON             : 0-second must-revalidate cache
  - Gzip (DEFLATE)              : Enabled for text, html, css, js, xml, fonts

================================================================================
3. DATABASE ARCHITECTURE & COMPLETE DATA DICTIONARY
================================================================================

Connection Layer: `app/database.php`
- Uses PHP PDO with strict error mode (`PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION`).
- Default Fetch Mode: `PDO::FETCH_ASSOC`.
- Native Prepares Enabled (`PDO::ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES => false`).
- Charset: `utf8mb4` with `utf8mb4_unicode_ci` collation.
- Dynamic error diagnostics for MySQL service down (2002), unknown DB (1049), and access denied (1045).

3.1 TABLE INVENTORY (23 Tables Total)
1.  `accounts`             : Client & user portal accounts (username, email, password hash, role: admin/manager/user/viewer, google_id).
2.  `admin`                : Primary administrative users for the admin dashboard.
3.  `registered_emails`    : Registered emails for verification, newsletter, and alerts.
4.  `modules`              : Toggle switch registry for application modules (blogs, leads, testimonials, etc.).
5.  `settings`             : Key-value global configuration store (site_name, logo, favicon, SMTP keys, map iframe, API keys).
6.  `uploads`              : Media library asset ledger (file_name, file_path, file_size, file_type, uploaded_by).
7.  `services`             : Digital marketing services catalog (title, slug, short_desc, full_desc, icon, thumbnail, status).
8.  `plans`                : Pricing packages and deliverables associated with services.
9.  `projects`             : Case studies and completed portfolio projects (title, client_name, results, thumbnail, status).
10. `testimonials`         : Client testimonials (client_name, company, rating, feedback, avatar, status).
11. `reviews`              : Public client reviews with star ratings (1-5) and approval moderation workflow (`pending`, `approved`, `rejected`).
12. `why_choose_us`        : Differentiating value proposition points shown on homepage and about sections.
13. `faqs`                 : Frequently Asked Questions categorized by topic with sorting order.
14. `pages`                : Custom CMS content pages (slug, title, body_content, meta_keywords, meta_description).
15. `leads`                : Inbound prospect inquiries captured from forms (name, phone, email, service, message, status: `new`, `contacted`, `confirmed`, `lose`).
16. `admin_activities`     : Granular audit trail for all admin operations (user_id, action, details, ip_address, user_agent, device_info, timestamp).
17. `admin_sessions`       : Active login sessions for tracking concurrent sessions and enforcing single-sign-on constraints.
18. `security_alerts`      : High-priority security warnings (brute-force detections, unauthorized access attempts).
19. `rate_limits`          : Persistent IP and action rate-limiting buckets.
20. `ip_blocks`            : Banned IP addresses blocked from submitting forms or accessing authentication endpoints.
21. `mail_logs`            : Transactional email history (recipient, subject, status: `sent`/`failed`, error_message, sent_at).
22. `mail_queue`           : Asynchronous outgoing email queue (recipient, subject, body_html, alt_body, attempts, max_attempts, status: `queued`/`processing`/`sent`/`failed`).
23. `blogs`                : Editorial blog posts (title, slug, excerpt, content, cover_image, category, tags, views, status: `draft`/`published`).

================================================================================
4. AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY ENGINE
================================================================================

4.1 SESSION MANAGEMENT & TIMEOUT
- Strict cookie parameters: `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`, `use_only_cookies=1`.
- Automatic HTTPS detection: sets cookie `secure` flag when HTTPS is active.
- Session regeneration every 30 minutes to prevent session fixation.
- Inactivity Timeout: `admin/auth.php` checks `$_SESSION['last_activity']`; automatically destroys session and redirects to `/admin/login?timeout=1` after 1800 seconds (30 minutes) of inactivity.

4.2 CSRF DEFENSE
- Functions in `app/config.php`:
  - `generateCSRFToken()`: Cryptographically secure 32-byte hex token stored with 1-hour expiration.
  - `verifyCSRFToken(?string $token)`: Constant-time comparison using `hash_equals()`.
  - `csrfField()`: Generates hidden input tag for seamless embedding into HTML forms.

4.3 AUDIT TRAIL & LOGGING
- `logAudit(PDO $conn, string $action, string $details, ?int $user_id)`:
  - Logs IP address via `getClientIP()` (honors Cloudflare `HTTP_CF_CONNECTING_IP` and trusted proxies).
  - Categorizes user agent into Desktop, Mobile, or Tablet with browser identifier.
  - Inserts directly into `admin_activities`.

4.4 ENCRYPTION AT REST
- Two-way AES-256-CBC cipher with SHA-256 key derivation:
  - `encryptSensitive(string $plaintext)`: Generates a random 16-byte IV, encrypts plaintext, and returns base64 string (`IV + Ciphertext`).
  - `decryptSensitive(string $encoded)`: Unpacks IV and decrypts ciphertext. Used for SMTP credentials and third-party API secrets.

4.5 INPUT SANITIZATION & RATE LIMITING
- Recursive string sanitization (`sanitize()` with `htmlspecialchars(..., ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')`).
- File path sanitization (`sanitizeFilename()`) removing traversal sequences `..` and illegal characters.
- Session-based and database-backed rate limiting (`checkRateLimit()`) preventing brute force submissions on contact and login forms.

4.6 SERVER-LEVEL HARDENING (.htaccess)
- Denial of direct HTTP access to sensitive extensions:
  `.env`, `.log`, `.ini`, `.conf`, `.git`, `.sql`, `.bak`, `.md`, `.sh`, `.zip`, `.phar`, `.lock`, `.json`
- Directory browsing disabled (`Options -Indexes`).
- Security Headers:
  - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
  - `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`
  - `X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block`
  - `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`
  - `Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), microphone=(), camera=()`

================================================================================
5. EMAIL, WHATSAPP & ASYNCHRONOUS QUEUE PIPELINE
================================================================================

5.1 SMTP FACTORY (`app/smtp_factory.php`)
- Centralized PHPMailer 7.1 configuration manager.
- Resolves IPv6 vs IPv4 issues common on shared hosting (e.g. NinzaHost / cPanel) via DNS lookup `resolveSmtpHostIPv4()` rather than fragile socket bindto.
- Automatically decrypts stored SMTP passwords.
- Anti-Spam Optimizations:
  - Clears `XMailer` header to prevent PHPMailer fingerprint spam scoring.
  - Sets custom Message-ID host and Return-Path sender domain for SPF/DKIM/DMARC alignment.
  - Implements `htmlToCleanPlainText()` for high-deliverability multipart MIME bodies.
- Resilience:
  - `sendWithRetry()`: Exponential backoff with up to 3 attempts, smart detection of permanent 5xx/auth errors to abort redundant attempts.

5.2 ASYNCHRONOUS QUEUE & WORKER
- `app/mail_queue.php`:
  - `enqueueMail()`: Inserts email payload into `mail_queue` table for non-blocking UI response times.
- `app/queue_worker.php`:
  - Worker process (executable via cPanel Cron: `php -q /home/.../app/queue_worker.php`).
  - Fetches pending batches, locks rows, sends via `smtp_factory`, logs result into `mail_logs`, and marks queue entries as sent or failed.

5.3 WHATSAPP INTEGRATION
- `app/services/WhatsAppService.php` & `app/whatsapp_helper.php`:
  - Dispatches instant WhatsApp notifications to agency administrators upon new lead submission.
  - Configurable in `admin/settings/integration.php`.

================================================================================
6. REST & AJAX API ENDPOINTS
================================================================================

6.1 PUBLIC API ENDPOINTS
- `POST /api/lead-capture.php`
  - Request: `name`, `phone`/`mobile`, `email`, `service`, `website`, `message`
  - Validates contact details, normalizes phone numbers.
  - Saves lead into `leads` table with status `new`.
  - Fires background email alerts (`sendLeadNotification`), thank-you emails (`sendLeadThankYouEmail`), and WhatsApp alert (`sendLeadWhatsAppAlert`).
  - Returns JSON `{status: "success"|"error", message: "..."}`.
- `GET /api/services.php`
  - Returns JSON array of all active digital marketing services.
- `GET /api/testimonials.php`
  - Returns JSON array of approved client testimonials and ratings.

6.2 ADMIN AJAX API ENDPOINTS
- `POST /admin/api/controller.php`
  - Master AJAX CRUD router for leads, services, testimonials, FAQs, and settings.
- `POST /admin/api/files.php`
  - Uploads images, verifies MIME types and extensions, generates unique names, inserts record into `uploads` table, and returns asset URL.
- `GET /admin/api/notifications.php`
  - Polling endpoint returning count of new unread leads and security alerts for dashboard badge indicators.
- `GET /admin/api/search.php`
  - Omnisearch query across leads, services, and blogs for the top navigation bar.
- `POST /admin/api/whatsapp.php`
  - Sends test WhatsApp messages to verify gateway credentials.
- `GET /admin/api/email_preview.php`
  - Renders HTML email templates with dummy data for visual testing before broadcast.

================================================================================
7. ADMIN CMS MODULES & SETTINGS HIERARCHY
================================================================================

7.1 DASHBOARD (`/admin/dashboard.php`)
- Real-time KPI Metric Cards: Total Leads, Active Services, Approved Reviews, Why Choose Us Items, Staff Count.
- 7-Day Inbound Lead Velocity Chart.
- Top Services demand distribution breakdown.
- Recent Leads table with inline status toggles.
- Real-time Audit Activity feed.

7.2 LEADS CRM (`/admin/leads.php`)
- Status Workflow:
  - `new`        : Newly captured lead, needs initial response.
  - `contacted`  : Outreach initiated via call/WhatsApp/email.
  - `confirmed`  : Lead qualified and converted to active client.
  - `lose`       : Lead unqualified or dropped out.
- Quick filters, CSV export, inline notes, and communication action links.

7.3 CONTENT CMS MODULES
- Services (`/admin/services.php`): Title, slug, icon, short summary, detailed deliverables, status.
- Blogs (`/admin/blogs.php`): Article title, slug, content, tags, featured image, SEO meta tags.
- Projects (`/admin/projects.php`): Portfolio case studies with client name, campaign results, and imagery.
- Reviews (`/admin/reviews.php`): Direct moderation queue to approve or decline client ratings.
- Testimonials (`/admin/testimonials.php`): Client quotes and ratings.
- Why Choose Us (`/admin/why-choose-us.php`): Core competitive advantages.
- FAQs (`/admin/faqs.php`): FAQ items with sorting order.
- Pages (`/admin/pages.php`): Custom legal and informational pages.

7.4 SYSTEM & SETTINGS ENGINE (`/admin/settings/`)
- General Settings      : Site Title, Favicon, Header Logo, Contact Email, Contact Phone, WhatsApp Number, Business Hours.
- Appearance Settings   : Active Theme (SaaS Pro, Enterprise, Light), primary color schemes.
- Integration Settings  : Google Maps Embed URL / API Key, Google Analytics ID, WhatsApp Gateway Token.
- Mail Settings         : SMTP Host, Port, Protocol (TLS/SSL), Username, Encrypted Password, Sender Name, Test Mail Tool.
- Module Switcher       : Global toggle to activate or deactivate modules across frontend and admin.
- Backup Manager        : Automated & one-click manual database backup engine (`admin/model/backup/BackupModel.php`) with archive pruning.

================================================================================
8. ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION & DEPLOYMENT GUIDELINES
================================================================================

8.1 ENVIRONMENT FILE (`app/.env`)
Structure:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_NAME=qaschyan_cloudaspire
DB_USER=qaschyan_cloudaspire
DB_PASS=qaschyan_cloudaspire
DB_CHARSET=utf8mb4

SITE_URL=https://cloudaspire.in
SITE_NAME="Cloud Aspire"
ENCRYPTION_KEY="random_32_character_hex_key"

SMTP_HOST=portel.cloudaspire.in
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=noreply@cloudaspire.in
SMTP_PASS=your_smtp_password
SMTP_FROM=noreply@cloudaspire.in
SMTP_FROM_NAME="Cloud Aspire"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8.2 LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ON XAMPP
1. Place repository in `c:\xampp\htdocs`.
2. Start Apache and MySQL from XAMPP Control Panel.
3. If using default MySQL root with no password, adjust `app/.env`:
   `DB_USER=root`, `DB_PASS=`.
4. Import `database_migration.sql` or run `http://localhost/migrate.php` in browser.
5. Access site at `http://localhost` and admin at `http://localhost/admin`.

8.3 PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT (cPanel / Apache)
1. Ensure PHP version is 8.2 or 8.4 (`ea-php84`).
2. Run `composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader`.
3. Set appropriate permissions: `uploads/` and `backups/` directories must be writable (`755` or `775`).
4. Ensure `.htaccess` is present in document root for URL rewriting and security headers.
5. Configure Cron Job for asynchronous email dispatch:
   `* * * * * /usr/local/bin/php /home/user/public_html/app/queue_worker.php > /dev/null 2>&1`
6. Verify SMTP Host is `portel.cloudaspire.in` on Port 587 (TLS).

